      ⍝ Bugs37 #83(f): integer printf conversions need a near-int B
      ⍝ (rounded), not a C-style truncation
      ⍝





      '%d' ⎕FIO[58] 2.99999999999999
3




      '%d %x' ⎕FIO[58] 1 2.5
DOMAIN ERROR+
      '%d %x' ⎕FIO[58]1 2.5
      ^       ^




      )MORE
B[2] (= 2.5) is not an integer, as required by format '%x' in A ⎕FIO.snprintf B




